# @description: Class organization and structure guidelines.

# Class Structure Guidelines

## Namespace Organization
- Use semicolons to join class namespaces (e.g., `class Marketing::BuyflowUrlBuilder`)
- Avoid nested module/class definitions
- Keep namespace hierarchy clear and concise

## Section Organization
- Use double hash marks (##) for section headers
- Organize sections in this order:
  ## ASSOCIATIONS
  ## VALIDATIONS
  ## DELEGATIONS
  ## PROPERTIES
  ## CLASS METHODS
  ## INSTANCE METHODS - PUBLIC
  ## INSTANCE METHODS - PRIVATE
  ## NESTED CLASSES

## Method Organization
- Alphabetize methods within each section
- Include a blank line between methods
- Group related methods together within sections
- Place private/protected methods after public ones
- Use consistent method naming conventions

## Examples

✅ Correct:
```ruby
class Marketing::BuyflowUrlBuilder
  ## ASSOCIATIONS
  belongs_to :campaign
  has_many :variants

  ## VALIDATIONS
  validates :campaign_id, presence: true
  validates :url, presence: true

  ## CLASS METHODS
  def self.find_by_campaign(campaign_id)
    # ...
  end

  ## INSTANCE METHODS - PUBLIC
  def generate_url
    # ...
  end

  ## INSTANCE METHODS - PRIVATE
  private

  def validate_url_format
    # ...
  end
end
```

❌ Incorrect:
- Nested module/class definitions
- Inconsistent section ordering
- Mixed method visibility
- Poor method organization
